WEBVTT

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:13.500
You're Avrora...

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.310
Senpai, what's wrong?

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.790
Uh, nothing.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:22.400
Geez, Kojou-kun.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.650
You shouldn't get charmed just 
because December-san is a beauty.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.290
It's not like that.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.880
Sorry that my little sister caused you a problem.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.440
No problem.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.980
I'd help out a cutie like her anytime.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.150
How peaceful.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:39.640
Huh?

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:44.480
Even after the bombing, there's a lot of food in the shops like nothing happened,

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.350
and there's people eating it.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:50.640
I was thinking food is directly connected to peace.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.360
Don't you think so?

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.240
Yeah.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.470
See ya, Nagisa-chan.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.120
Kojou-kun, bye, bye.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:04.990
Ah, Kojou-kun, what about the milk?

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:06.970
Sorry, I haven't looked for it yet.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:10.900
Geez, you said you'd buy some—you're beyond help.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:13.170
Ah, there might be some in <i>that</i> shop.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.740
I'll look into it.

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:19.140
Seems like Nagisa is back to her old self.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.250
Yes. Thank God.

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:24.420
"Food is connected to peace," huh?

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:25.100
Hm?

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:27.170
<i>It's terrorism.</i>

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:30.980
<i>With the aim of causing mayhem on Itogami Island, and annihilating it.</i>

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.940
Tartarus Lapse's next target.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:35.770
What?

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:41.530
December said food is directly connected to peace.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:46.160
If Tartarus Lapse's goal is to put Itogami Island into disorder...

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.220
Don't tell me.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.240
It's just a theory.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.380
But I feel something bad is coming.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:02:00.010
Their next target is probably the large-scale food supply reserve storehouse in Great Pile, Island East.

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:41.350
Well done figuring out this place, Minamiya Natsuki.

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:46.210
One of my students is great 
at searching for people, you see.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.900
It's been 15 years since then, huh?

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.740
And you still look the same.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:53.760
You bastard though, have aged, Senga Takehito.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.550
Are you still abusing children?

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:01.380
I merely taught them how to use their powers.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:04.600
Just like you did in the olden days.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:09.350
Are you saying the annihilation of the special 
administrative region for demons is the children's will?

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:14.350
To prove that, I'm not even Tartarus Lapse's leader.

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:16.580
Their commander is someone else.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.150
Oh, interesting...

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:23.320
But first, I need to destroy the
 Eight Trigrams Formation you set.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:26.030
<i>After</i> that will I see what you bastards have to say.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:35.820
It sure gets cold at night.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:39.560
Yes. A good thing we brought jackets.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.040
It's beautiful and refreshing.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.410
I can't even take my eyes off it.

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:47.640
S-Senpai, what're you saying out of the blue?

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:50.600
Hm? So <i>your</i> feelings aren't <i>that</i> strong?

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:53.910
Well, I <i>do</i> like it, but...

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:56.560
It was <i>Nagisa-chan</i> who chose the design...

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.560
Hm? What are you talking about?

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.280
Huh? What were <i>you</i> talking about?

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:07.470
Uh, this area was redeveloped recently,
 so I was thinking that the view at night is refreshing.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.830
U-Uhh, the "view"?

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:11.360
Is that so?

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:13.200
Makes sense.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:16.720
But it was redeveloped because of you to begin with, wasn't it?

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:22.050
You couldn't control the familiar, 
so you turned everything to ash.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:23.760
What could I do?

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.860
That was still before I sucked your blood.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:28.180
Right.

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:35.020
It looks like you're not just sucking my blood anymore, but snacking on other girls too.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:37.770
Hold it!

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.230
Why'd you pull your spear now?!

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:44.230
What's with this crazy mana?

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:54.790
You're currently incapable of stopping 
the Rose of Tartarus, Minamiya Natsuki!

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:55.910
You bastard!

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:59.420
A golem that can control wind storms and ocean waves!

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.670
Don't tell me—those are Stone Warriors!

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:06.090
Come, Al-Nasl-Minium!

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.530
It's regenerating?

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:17.440
Damn, this is never gonna end!

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.580
I'll defeat the spellcaster!

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:23.870
You buy me some time please.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:28.360
Sorry, but I guess I can't let you do that.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:31.070
December-san?

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:38.920
Now it's in your hands.

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:46.900
Don't tell me you're a comrade of the Tartarus Lapse.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.480
A "comrade," huh?

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:50.720
It has a nice ring to it.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.640
Just so you know, I'm the leader.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:57.440
The Fourth Progenitor, Akatsuki Kojou.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:00.160
How do you feel about 
turning into one of our comrades?

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:01.920
We'd welcome the girl behind you too.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:02.860
Fuck off!

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.060
That so? Too bad.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:10.990
It's a D-Type.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.280
Damn it.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:14.030
Al-Nasl-Minium!

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:19.370
Draw back, Al-Nasl-Minium.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.000
Senpai, what on Earth just happened?

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:26.880
Senpai!

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:48.820
To think you can mind-control the Fourth Progenitor...

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:51.070
What are you?

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.920
"Mind-control"?

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:57.430
Do not be concerned about Akatsuki Kojou's familiar, transfer student.

00:07:57.430 --> 00:07:59.580
That woman is your opponent.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:08.390
I, Sword Shaman of the High God and priestess of the Lion,

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:11.970
beseech thee. Spirit wolf of snowy mist, fashion a shield from the echoes

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:15.100
of the thousand swift ones, and expel this calamity!

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:31.110
Senpai!

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.070
Seems it's cancelled.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:38.030
Whatever, our goal has been completed.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:41.000
Your "goal... has been completed"?

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:51.090
An ignition esper... a pyrokinesist?

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:54.850
The perpetrator in the Keystone Gate bombing, huh?

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:59.850
So both Senga's Stone Warriors and 
you bastard were decoys for him, huh?

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.770
I shall allow no more!

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:09.440
Good grief, you leave me no choice.

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:14.900
I didn't want to hurt Takehito's 
friends more than needed.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:16.990
Carly, it's your turn.

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:24.410
A curse-type... bullet?

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.360
Natsuki-chan!

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.460
Minamiya-sensei!

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:34.070
I'll ask you for the last time—

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:37.430
Akatsuki Kojou, join us.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:42.310
After this, I can't possibly say yes to that!

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.390
It's our party of change.

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:51.110
Since those desiring power toyed with your fate, just like with that of us,

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:54.570
I was certain you'd understand.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.720
What do you know?

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:02.330
It looks like you still haven't remembered everything.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:04.620
I guess I'll have to use force...

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:08.320
Come, Natra-Cinereus!

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:20.520
A camouflage?

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:23.280
I'd expect nothing less of the boy she <i>chose</i>.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:26.300
Let's retreat, Rogi, Carly.

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:28.190
The Rose's preparations are done.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:37.660
Hey, Nina.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:40.320
She suffered exorbitant damage,

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:44.540
so do you think Natsuki-chan's real body is alright inside the Prison Barrier?

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:48.000
Well, the person herself is unwounded.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:53.250
Though with the spiritual object the way it is,
 the impact of the destruction probably got through.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:57.890
It'll take a while before she can move in here.

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:59.340
Is that so?

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:03.300
Astarte, any instructions from Natsuki-chan?

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:07.430
One corresponding entry found.

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:12.150
"Investigate regarding the Rose of Tartarus."

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:14.390
"The Rose of Tartarus"?

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:16.610
Sorry for making you wait.

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:23.250
Thanks, Kanase.

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:25.330
Sorry we didn't help.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:29.580
It's fine, it helped keep my mind off things.

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.540
Don't be shy, dig in.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.950
The transport ships...

00:11:32.110 --> 00:11:37.000
We don't know how much longer food will be available on this island, after all.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.090
...the large-scale conflagration.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:39.970
Consequently...

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:50.080
I don't mind that classes are cancelled but couldn't they have sent the notice earlier?

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:52.940
I hardly managed to sleep and 
forced myself to wake up...

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:56.650
The island's administration is in great disorder, you know.

00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:00.030
The teachers in the school are tied up with work as well—

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:02.360
Oh, you've got a message from Kojou-niichan.{or just "Kojou"?}

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:07.750
It says "I want you to investigate the Rose of Tartarus."

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:10.880
I thought he's worried about me for once, and yet...

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:14.690
What does that jerk think of me?

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:16.970
You lost the moment you had your hopes up, missy.

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:18.090
You're annoying!

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:21.410
Anyway, did you look into it.

00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:22.100
So?

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:25.050
Not much corresponding to it in the public corporation archives.

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:30.520
We could sink into other intelligence agencies too, but that would obviously take a lot of time.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:32.460
I'll just have to do it myself.

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:35.900
Tell Kojou "Wait a bit, I'll look into it."

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:39.430
Also add that "I'm going to see how things are at Motoki's place,

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:41.740
so you can come too, if you're not too busy."

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:42.610
Right, right.

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:48.490
That person is... if I'm not mistaken.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:51.450
Are you visiting him too?

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:54.420
You're Motoki's senior, right?

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:02.820
I-It's not like that!

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:08.090
I'm just his childhood friend, I'm not his girlfriend or anything like that at all!

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:10.100
Geez...

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:14.060
Argh, she completely misunderstood...

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:18.910
This doesn't feel right.

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:22.030
It's like the calm before the storm.

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:24.980
You could cut the air with a spear.

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:27.450
It's my responsibility.

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:30.910
It's because I couldn't protect the Great Pile.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.500
C'mon, what makes you say that?

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:36.250
It's not your job to guard the storehouse, Himeragi.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:40.060
But I'm a Sword Shaman of the Lion King Organization.

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:42.710
An <i>apprentice</i> Sword Shaman, aren't you?

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:47.180
U-Um, Senpai.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:59.210
I told you about what happened 
when I used to play basketball, right?

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:00.360
Yes.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:04.820
When December hijacked
 my familiar, I remembered that.

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:10.600
Being called the strongest vampire in the world 
made me full of myself, and look what happened

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:13.790
But you couldn't help it.

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:19.880
I know how you feel, but feeling down won't achieve anything.

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:23.420
The next time we face them it'll be then or never.

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:26.760
This is my fight now.

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:28.970
No, Senpai.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:31.180
This is <i>our</i> fight.

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:41.470
But I still don't know how I should feel about December.

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:47.530
I feel like my heart is torn up whenever I see her.

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:58.960
If you want to know more about December, come with us for a bit,

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:00.370
Fourth Progenitor.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:03.520
You're the one who blew up the storehouse yesterday.

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:06.550
Just call me "Rogi," Akatsuki Kojou.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:11.240
Our master, Senga Takehito wants to talk.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:12.700
Did I hear that right?

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:14.430
As a matter of fact, Carly,

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:17.300
the sniper has her scope set on you guys now.

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:20.940
I wonder if a stray bullet or 
two will hit someone unrelated.

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:26.710
Where do we need to go?

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:27.860
Senpai!

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:30.510
You'll see soon.

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:33.850
Don't expect too much hospitality, though.

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:47.190
Fourth Progenitor, you were wise to come.

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:47.880
You have my thanks.

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:50.030
Are you the one called Senga Takehito?

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:51.090
That's correct.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:54.880
So you're the geomancer who put Itogami Island under a blockade, I take it.

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:57.350
Well, I can't deny it was my job.

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:01.270
She's Rahn, one of our comrades.

00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:03.730
So they're all kids?

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:10.880
It might sound like an excuse, but I'm not forcing them.

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:14.390
The barrier on the special administrative region for demons was their wish.

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:15.240
What?

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:22.210
Take Rogi as an example: He was born as a pyrokinesist, a military-use homunculus experiment.

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:23.740
"Experiment"?

00:16:23.740 --> 00:16:25.920
A body modification with military objective?

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:27.920
It's illegal, of course.

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:33.090
December came around to save him, when his state was revealed and he was about to be disposed of.

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:36.510
In the town formerly called the Iroise special administrative region for demons.

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:41.660
It was, well, more or less the same for the other kids too.

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:44.680
Is that why they're so keen on ruining Itogami Island?

00:16:44.680 --> 00:16:46.480
'Cause it's a region for demons too?

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:47.680
Wrong.

00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:51.180
There's a particular reason that 
this town became their goal.

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:52.240
"Reason"?

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:55.480
That's exactly why I called you here.

00:16:55.480 --> 00:17:01.160
They wish you will be willing to cooperate 
with us, once you get aware of the reason.

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:04.120
I already told you I'm sorry.

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:10.050
I never expected I'd bump into what's her name, Hiina-san?

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:15.490
But bringing all these fruits to you...
 She's a little strange.

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:17.520
Whatever, they're tasty.

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:18.510
Damn...

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:21.960
Well, you too were kind enough to worry about me,

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:24.040
so I <i>am</i> grateful.

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:25.980
Yep, better be grateful.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:31.150
So, how did your father's rescue operations go?

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:33.200
No news yet.

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:36.860
Their hands are probably full, 
having to restore the Great Pile.

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:38.540
How worrisome.

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:43.100
The only reason your father became the terrorists' target is that he's an authority on the island, right?{The only reason your father became the terrorists' target is that he's the island's leader, right?}{Not necessarily _the_ leader, just one of the top men. Though if you found somewhere in the novels that he's actually _the_ leader and Asagi knows it, then you can forget what I wrote.}

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:44.870
Probably.

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:48.700
But there's many things I simply can't accept.

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:50.260
What do you mean?

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:52.920
My brothers are operating the island in practice.

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:55.090
If someone wanted to wreak havoc on it,

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:58.340
choosing my father as a target would be strange.

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:02.000
Besides, if he would die from an explosion like that...

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:05.810
Well, he had dozens of chances to kick the bucket long before.

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:13.770
I'll say it first hand: I have no intention of cooperating with you all.

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:16.360
I ain't gonna give a hand to murderers.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:18.340
"Murderers," you say?

00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:22.370
The same could be said to those who made this island, though.

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:25.650
As for the next tragedy this island is going to cause,

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:30.330
the number of victims there will be order of magnitude different than that of the people we killed.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:33.300
"The next tragedy the island is going to cause."

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:36.690
The true identity of the man-made island called Itogami Island

00:18:36.690 --> 00:18:40.260
is an altar to revive Cain the god-accursed.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:46.930
Itogami Island's designer, Itogami Senra, wished for Cain's revival.

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:51.040
He may have died, but those who inherited his ideology

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:54.320
still remain in Itogami Island's center.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:59.720
Then your assassination of the staff of the
 Manmade Island Management Corporation...

00:18:59.720 --> 00:19:03.330
was a terrorism for your great cause?

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:05.340
How is it, Fourth Progenitor?

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:08.140
Did you make up your mind to cooperate with us?

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:09.740
"Cooperate," huh?

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:11.780
Good grief.

00:19:11.780 --> 00:19:14.290
Everyone's the same, huh?

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:16.050
Senpai?

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:17.660
What do you mean by that?

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:22.190
Why do you have to burden yourself with everything?

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:26.210
You remind me of my former self—

00:19:26.210 --> 00:19:27.720
It's embarrassing.

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:30.890
You don't you ask for help?

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:32.310
Why don't you speak up?

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:34.350
And if you even run away into the world of terrorism,

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:36.320
just who exactly do you think will follow you?

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:39.280
Of course I <i>have</i> tried speaking up.

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:42.820
But it was crushed in front of their political power,

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:44.920
and even when something went through to them,

00:19:44.920 --> 00:19:49.530
no one believed me saying I have no clear proof.

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:51.370
Are you sure?

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:55.420
Is the reason they didn't believe you 
solely that you didn't have proof?

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:57.000
I bet it isn't!

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.800
Isn't that because <i>you all</i> didn't believe <i>them</i>?

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:01.010
What?

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:04.760
You said there'll be masses of victims once Cain's revived, didn't you?

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:09.020
Then what you must do isn't wrecking the special administrative region for demons,

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:11.140
but rescuing the victims-to-be!

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.290
Selfish brat.

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:16.740
No need for that, Rogi.

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:21.190
We're incompatible after all, huh?

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:25.380
But, very well, we've fulfilled our duty.

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:26.660
"Duty"?

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:29.040
We've no intention of changing our methods.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:33.880
It is our longstanding desire to 
revive Cain by direct means.

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:36.630
By obliterating his priest, that is.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:38.140
"Cain's priest"?

00:20:38.140 --> 00:20:39.590
You are not aware?

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:41.510
Aiba Asagi.

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:43.050
Your bosom buddy.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:47.760
Don't tell me you called us here to separate us from Aiba-senpai.

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:50.180
Senga!!

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:51.140
Senpai!

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:57.810
I won't ask you to forgive us, Fourth Progenitor.

00:20:57.810 --> 00:20:59.520
Feng Shui Technique, huh?

00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:01.780
Watch your head, Senpai!

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:14.360
Let's go.

00:21:14.360 --> 00:21:15.310
Yes!

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:22.120
At any rate, Kojou's late.

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:24.090
At this rate, there will be no melon for him.

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:26.220
So why on Earth are you eating it all—?

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:32.060
Asagi!

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:34.750
W-What the—?!

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:35.440
It's a sniper.

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:42.880
Incendiary explosives in the middle of the town?!

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:44.250
Are they nuts?

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:45.700
What's going on, geez?!

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:49.760
Damn, it ain't getting through.

00:21:50.320 --> 00:21:52.680
Senpai, where's Yaze-senpai's apartment?

00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:55.500
Two stops by monorail from here.

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:00.380
Himeragi!

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:01.630
Y-Yes.

00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:03.880
S-Senpai?

00:22:07.300 --> 00:22:09.010
This strength...

00:22:09.940 --> 00:22:12.060
is coming from that sword familiar.

00:22:12.550 --> 00:22:14.730
Have you learned to control it?

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:15.750
No.

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:17.310
I don't really understand it yet,

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:19.340
but I just felt like I could do it now.

00:22:19.340 --> 00:22:21.770
That's irresponsible.

00:22:27.940 --> 00:22:29.610
Senpai.

00:22:33.600 --> 00:22:35.050
It's all right.

00:22:35.050 --> 00:22:39.080
I'll never pull such an exhausting stunt again once we save Asagi.

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:43.170
What's that?

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:44.560
Must be Asagi!

00:22:52.860 --> 00:22:55.470
So you came, Akatsuki Kojou.

00:22:56.210 --> 00:22:58.690
Move it, December.

00:22:58.690 --> 00:23:02.390
Aiba Asagi must not stay alive.

00:23:02.390 --> 00:23:04.900
She's too dangerous.

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:08.030
Come, Regulus-Aurum!

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:11.950
Draw back, Regulus-Aurum!

00:23:16.060 --> 00:23:17.620
Come.

00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:23.980
Come, Mesarthim-Adamas,
 Al-Nasl-Minium, Al-Meissa Mercury!

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:32.430
Draw back, Mesarthim-Adamas,
 Al-Nasl-Minium, Al-Meissa Mercury!

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:40.940
Don't, Senpai!

00:23:40.940 --> 00:23:42.570
I'll handle her.

00:23:42.570 --> 00:23:43.940
So don't any more!

00:23:43.940 --> 00:23:46.320
Come, Kiffa-Ater!

00:23:51.470 --> 00:23:54.450
Draw back! You're of my womb!

00:23:55.650 --> 00:24:01.790
Come, Sadalmelik-Albus, Cor Tauri-Sucinum!

00:24:08.960 --> 00:24:09.800
Senpai!

00:24:12.030 --> 00:24:13.760
Are you...

00:24:13.760 --> 00:24:18.510
Are you going to kill me again?

00:24:18.510 --> 00:24:19.890
Akatsuki Kojou.

00:24:31.130 --> 00:24:32.950
Senpai!

00:24:35.810 --> 00:24:37.780
Well done, December.

00:24:37.780 --> 00:24:39.820
You've done plently.

00:24:40.750 --> 00:24:42.720
We ran out of time, Rahn.

00:24:42.720 --> 00:24:44.540
Set the Rose into motion.

00:24:51.130 --> 00:24:52.240
Senpai.

00:24:52.240 --> 00:24:53.520
Please pull yourself together!

00:24:53.520 --> 00:24:54.860
Senpai!
